<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-17">17 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Eisenhower warns of the 'military-industrial complex'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In his televised farewell address, the outgoing President cautioned that a permanent arms industry and huge defence establishment could acquire 'unwarranted influence' over American government.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-20">20 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">John F. Kennedy is inaugurated as US President</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At 43, Kennedy became the youngest person elected President. His inaugural address urged Americans to 'ask what you can do for your country'. He was assassinated less than three years later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-31">31 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ham the chimpanzee flies into space</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Ham flew a suborbital flight on Mercury-Redstone 2, performing simple tasks in response to lights. His safe return cleared the way for Alan Shepard's flight that May.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/prague" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prague.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-15">15 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US figure skating team killed in the Sabena air crash</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Sabena Flight 548 crashed on approach to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>, killing all 72 aboard and a man on the ground. Among the dead was the entire US figure skating team, en route to the world championships in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-11">11 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Adolf Eichmann's trial opens in Jerusalem</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Adolf Eichmann, a principal organiser of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>, went on trial in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. Survivor testimony broadcast worldwide shaped public understanding of the Holocaust; he was hanged in 1962.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-12">12 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Yuri Gagarin becomes the first human in space</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet cosmonaut <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-gagarin">Yuri Gagarin</a> orbited the Earth once aboard Vostok 1 in a flight of 108 minutes. The achievement gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> a major lead in the space race.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-17">17 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Cuban exiles land at the Bay of Pigs</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A CIA-trained brigade of some 1,400 Cuban exiles landed in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> to overthrow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>. They were defeated within three days, a grave embarrassment for the new Kennedy administration.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-5">5 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Alan Shepard becomes the first American in space</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Alan Shepard made a 15-minute suborbital flight in Freedom 7, three weeks after Gagarin's orbit. Twenty days later President Kennedy committed the US to landing a man on the Moon.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-25">25 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Kennedy commits America to landing on the Moon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Addressing Congress, President Kennedy called for a man to be landed on the Moon and returned safely before the decade was out. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo-11">Apollo 11</a> met the goal in July 1969.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-19">19 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Kuwait gains independence from Britain</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An exchange of notes ended the 1899 agreement that made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuwait">Kuwait</a> a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> claimed the new state, and invaded it in 1990.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-13">13 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">East Germany seals the border in Berlin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Overnight, East German forces closed the crossings and began building barriers that became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a>. For 28 years it divided the city, and at least 140 people died trying to cross.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hiroshima.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-30">30 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union tests the Tsar Bomba</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A Soviet bomber dropped the largest nuclear weapon ever exploded over Novaya Zemlya in the Arctic. Its yield of about 50 megatons was some 3,000 times that of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a> bomb.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-9">9 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tanganyika becomes independent</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Tanganyika became independent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> as prime minister. In 1964 it united with Zanzibar to form Tanzania.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-pigs-invasion" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bay-of-pigs-invasion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-pigs-invasion">Bay of Pigs invasion</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bay of Pigs invasion was a failed landing in southern Cuba on 17–20 April 1961 by about 1,400 Cuban exiles trained and funded by the CIA, aiming to overthrow Fidel Castro.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-hattie" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-hattie.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-hattie">Hurricane Hattie</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hurricane Hattie was a powerful hurricane that struck British Honduras on 31 October 1961.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/generals-putsch">Generals' Putsch</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Generals' Putsch was a failed coup in Algiers in April 1961 by four retired French generals, Maurice Challe, Edmond Jouhaud, André Zeller and Raoul Salan, who opposed Charles de Gaulle's move towards Algerian self-determination.</p></div></li></ol></section>
